I've been trying to adapt the repeated measures rats example (bugs examples vol. 1) to work using nested indexing to allow for unbalanced data. My model works in modified jags/bugs code but I can't seem to get it to work in Stan. I think the issue is in the data specification step in the model file. Here's my toy data, it's essentially in the long-format:

$Ndata
[1] 10

$Nsubj
[3] 3

$subj
[1] 1 1 1 1 2 2 2 3 3 3

$x
[1] 0 3 4 10 0 3 10 3 4 10

$y
[1] 2.1, 4, 4.4, 6, 2, 3.5, 5.9, 3.8, 4.3, 6.1

In the rats stan example, the data structure was specified as follows.

data{
    int<lower=0> N;   # number of subjects
    int<lower=0> K;   # number of timepoints where rat growth was measured
    real x[N];
    real y[N,K];
}

This is clearly not right for my data format, but I'm at a loss as to how to specify it correctly. Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Best,
  Ian

