>From reading the docs/watching the sampling output, my understanding is that rstan obtains iter number of samples (all of which are saved), with warmup number of those used for adapting the sampler. If this assumption is correct, how do I ignore the warmup samples that are saved when making inference (say for something as basic as printing the summary of the fit)? And is it possible to have rstan simply not save these warmup iterations?

