> parameter unconstrained but evaluated it mod 2pi there wouldn't be any
> issues.  Technically, this produces an improper distribution over R
> but I don't think it would cause a real problem.

I think I am misunderstanding something. In the von Mises distribution,

f(x | u,k) = e^( k * cos(x - u) ) / ( 2 * pi * I(k) )

if we substitute the random variable y := cos(x - u), constrain y to be on [-1,1], unwind to get the transformed parameter x = acos(y) + u, and deal with the change of variables, then what is the problem besides implementing the log of the Bessel function(s)?

> That said, distributions like the von Mises are one big motivation to
> implement a version of NUTS with nonlinear parameter constraints.

True.

Ben

