You are the second or third person to mention Kronecker products, so hopefully Stan will have a kronecker() function soon. I guess you are doing the Kronecker product by hand, in which case, yes it makes sense wherever possible to manipulate the smaller blocks. Basically, anytime you have to do an O(K^3) matrix decomposition, stop and think if there might be a shortcut.

As regards to the manual, hopefully everything I said will be obsolete soon. Once we have a covariance matrix class in C++, then it will just be a matter of specifying inherited classes with various special structures.

Ben

