Damn. Yesterday was not a good day. The transformed parameter in question is tau, not gamma, although it was given a gamma distribution in the example. So, this should have said:

If you are going to use informative priors, Stan makes you apply them to things in the parameters block only. However, since

p(sigma | ...) \propto abs(det( J[sigma -> tau] )) * p(tau | ...)

a specification for p(tau | ...) commits you to a specification for p(sigma | ...) but you have to adjust the log posterior yourself. In this case, the Jacobian is 1x1, so it is just the partial derivative of tau with respect to sigma (which I totally messed up twice, so far).

